'''Elections to [[Stevenage Borough Council]]''' took place on 5 May 2022.<ref>{{Cite web|url=https://www.stevenage.gov.uk/council-and-democracy/elections-and-voting/2022-election/election-results-borough-council-elections-2022 |title=Election Results - Borough Council Elections 2022 |access-date=10 May 2022 |work=Stevenage Borough Council}}</ref> This was on the same day as other [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|local elections]] across the [[United Kingdom]]. One third of the council was up for election; the seats which were last contested in [[2018 Stevenage Borough Council election|2018]]. The [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour Party]] retained control of the council, which it has held continuously since its creation in 1973.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/election/2022/england/councils/E07000243|publisher=BBC News|title=Stevenage election result}}</ref>

